'' The conversion family over a fixed zstring and over a UDT that extends zstring.
'' Both shapes ICEd in the EMITTER, which '--dump-ir' never reaches -- see the source.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/conv-string-operand.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered

'' The VAL family is reached at all now. It was reached for neither operand before.
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_VALINT
'' EXPECT-OUT: declare f64 fb_VAL(ptr $0)
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_VALBOOL

'' The UDT's cast result is a bare char*, so it borrows a temporary descriptor before
'' the VAL call. Without this the runtime read a descriptor out of string data and
'' 'clng( u )' answered 0 for a UDT holding "42" -- a wrong ANSWER, not a crash, which
'' would have outlived the ICE fix in silence.
'' EXPECT-OUT: fb_StrAllocTempDescZ

'' Built and RUN against fbc on the same source: both print
''     42  42 / 42  42 / 42  42 / true  true
'' GOLDEN: expected/conv-string-operand.out
